{# IN·07 — six months of filings, the line the map cannot draw.

   The one reading on this surface whose window is not the page's month: the map,
   the register and every other chart read the one month, but a trend needs more
   than a month to be a line, so the repository carries its own six
   ({@see IncidentRepository::monthlyFiledCounts}). One filter still drives it —
   the category chips, the lens and the search narrow the line the same way they
   narrow the register.

   THE DRAWING IS THE ATLAS'S. This module states a kind and a series
   ({@see IncidentDashboard::trendChart}) and writes one line of Twig; the
   colours, the grid, the axes, the legend and the height are the component's,
   so this line and every other line in the product read the same way. It drew
   its own SVG until the ruling that the atlas owns every module visual. #}
<div class="c" data-w="trend">
    {{ atlas_chart(dashboard.trendChart, 'Incidents over time') }}
</div>
